From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:44:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: edp: Program the v8 TX2/TX3 lane control at its v8
 offset

The v8 eDP PHY sequence writes the TX2/TX3 lane control value to 0xa0,
the DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL offset of the v4 and v6 PHYs. Several eDP
PHY registers sit 4 bytes above their counterparts in the combo PHY's
DP_PHY block (VCO_DIV 0x74 vs 0x70, TSYNC_OVRD 0x78 vs 0x74,
TX0_TX1_LANE_CTL 0x7c vs 0x78, AUXLESS_CFG1 0xcc vs 0xc8, LFPS_PERIOD
0xd4 vs 0xd0), and so does TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL on v4 (0xa0 vs 0x9c). On v8
the combo PHY's TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL moved to 0xbc, which puts this one at
0xc0. The sequence that drives the Surface Laptop 8 panel at 5.4 Gbps
programs 0x05 at 0xc0 and leaves 0xa0 alone.

Program TX2/TX3 lane control at 0xc0 on v8 and stop writing 0xa0 there.
The v4 and v6 sequences are unchanged.

Fixes: add66a6673bc ("phy: qcom: edp: Add Glymur platform support")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
index c5d1fa0ae6c..2edfd2e566a 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 #define DP_PHY_TSYNC_OVRD                       0x0078
 #define DP_PHY_TX0_TX1_LANE_CTL                 0x007c
 #define DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL                 0x00a0
+#define DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL_V8              0x00c0
 #define DP_PHY_AUXLESS_CFG1                     0x00cc
 #define DP_PHY_LFPS_PERIOD                      0x00d4
 #define DP_PHY_LFPS_CYC                         0x00d8
@@ -1470,7 +1471,7 @@ static int qcom_edp_configure_tx_pre_pll_v46(const struct qcom_edp *edp)
 static int qcom_edp_configure_tx_pre_pll_v8(const struct qcom_edp *edp)
 {
 	writel(0x05, edp->edp + DP_PHY_TX0_TX1_LANE_CTL);
-	writel(0x05, edp->edp + DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL);
+	writel(0x05, edp->edp + DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL_V8);
 
 	return qcom_edp_configure_tx_pre_pll_v8_lanes(edp);
 }
